# Refresh token JWT (~1 year lifetime). This is the `usr` cookie from a
# signed-in zola.com session. Two ways to provide it:
#   1. Leave this unset and use the fetchproxy extension (recommended) — the
#      server reads the cookie from your signed-in zola.com tab on first call.
#   2. Sign in at zola.com, copy the `usr` cookie via DevTools (Application →
#      Cookies → https://www.zola.com), and paste the value below.
# See "Getting your refresh token" in the README for details.
ZOLA_REFRESH_TOKEN=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...

# Optional overrides — auto-resolved from GET /v3/users/me/context if not set.
# ZOLA_ACCOUNT_ID=1234567
# ZOLA_REGISTRY_ID=abc123def456
# ZOLA_WEDDING_ID=7654321

# Optional: short-lived session token (30 min). Skips the initial refresh call.
# Not needed if ZOLA_REFRESH_TOKEN is set — the server auto-refreshes.
# ZOLA_SESSION_TOKEN=
